{"uuid":"F69FABB0-FA69-5F02-A36F-5A43B5F2FD24","name":"Buffalo Chicken Bowls","serves":10,"duration":10,"cookingDuration":290,"defaultScale":1,"isPublicRecipe":false,"folderIDs":[],"ingredients":[{"uuid":"5BA6EB7E-24B7-5AFB-ACE8-0427F80DA103","order":0,"ingredient":{"uuid":"78C2EBC2-B234-5FC4-8863-35E596881E5F","name":"chicken breast, whole (not cubed)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"POUND","amount":5.25}},{"uuid":"2BE4651B-A8D4-5A51-BF07-08E5295BFF2C","order":1,"ingredient":{"uuid":"A5FB4E64-B2E8-50EE-B561-22B714938723","name":"chicken broth"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"22A800B9-C6E5-5FFB-AD5B-E1154DA175BA","order":2,"ingredient":{"uuid":"0246DCB7-FDE4-597A-8390-75ED1BC7A745","name":"Frank's RedHot"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":0.6667}},{"uuid":"7073A0DA-445D-5B44-901C-7195D5118BCB","order":3,"ingredient":{"uuid":"1B394667-CBD9-53CE-A9F0-F9248F40EA6C","name":"butter"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":6}},{"uuid":"4E458269-686A-5E67-A3B9-B1889ED9170C","order":4,"ingredient":{"uuid":"42E72D37-C2CE-59ED-B750-081FF92909A2","name":"white vinegar"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TABLESPOON","amount":2}},{"uuid":"8F813FB1-CA87-591F-A133-B8AE314E609A","order":5,"ingredient":{"uuid":"FCC6150F-6005-54B1-9776-37D9B033B9AA","name":"cayenne pepper (optional)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":0.5}},{"uuid":"EC83C7E5-A0E5-5943-8D86-8F1C326D49DB","order":6,"ingredient":{"uuid":"A29561BC-5FBF-5106-AC98-97D534E2F198","name":"garlic powder"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"TEASPOON","amount":1}},{"uuid":"75A37068-9A83-5973-B5E8-017A07809304","order":7,"ingredient":{"uuid":"464B5AEC-ED5E-5E1F-A3E7-630FC02A7B71","name":"jasmine rice (dry)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"CUP","amount":3.25}},{"uuid":"2E965D11-9DE3-5497-92CF-67EA54C7BA04","order":8,"ingredient":{"uuid":"68728623-9782-5FDE-8DCA-D29FD2411CE1","name":"bags frozen broccoli florets (~1000 g total)"},"quantity":{"quantityType":"ITEM","amount":3}},{"uuid":"0CB99969-EE96-559B-90EF-E4557B349664","order":9,"ingredient":{"uuid":"CF641923-63CC-5076-A9B5-10686FEC24F3","name":"Salt, pepper"}},{"uuid":"A6E0D6B4-0EE3-5D84-851A-110387EA75E7","order":10,"ingredient":{"uuid":"7CC7360C-5C4F-57C1-A304-721EDAE26225","name":"Ranch or blue cheese dressing, diced celery (added fresh when eating)"}}],"steps":[{"uuid":"FD5B9E53-9DB2-5639-9A7E-CC7F6E3D6256","order":0,"step":"Place ~5 ¼ lbs whole chicken breasts in the crockpot. Season with salt and pepper and add ½ cup chicken broth. No cutting required.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"5AB42C17-08A2-5411-B4F4-D13BAB309118","order":1,"step":"Cook on High 4–5 hours, or Low 7–8 hours. Do not open the lid to check before hour 4 — each peek adds 15–20 minutes.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"ABD3FC03-5B4C-5E65-A2F8-4EE531F60FB5","order":2,"step":"Test for shreddability rather than for temperature. Chicken is food-safe at 165°F but will not pull apart until roughly 195–205°F, when the connective tissue breaks down. Pull a piece and try it with two forks; if it holds together in a chunk, give it another 30 minutes.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"A0675F1D-9AA1-58AC-B4C7-308C749A5A34","order":3,"step":"Drain the cooking liquid, reserving ¾ cup. Draining first is what keeps the sauce from being watered down.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"39A94881-77DC-5FB2-87D8-D1B2A46CDD9F","order":4,"step":"Shred the chicken with a hand mixer directly in the crockpot — about 30 seconds. A few pulses only; over-mixing turns it mushy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"AC4EA221-A273-5B84-B7BF-B8ECAB3F1751","order":5,"step":"Melt 6 tbsp butter, then whisk in ⅔ cup Frank's RedHot, 1 tsp garlic powder, the cayenne, and the ¾ cup reserved liquid.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"C34A8110-811A-579A-82BF-AC5C78219CF5","order":6,"step":"Remove the sauce from the heat and stir in 2 tbsp white vinegar. The acid goes in last, and here it is doing a specific job — see Notes.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"50D160E0-F638-5C80-BE99-AA317ED6A83A","order":7,"step":"Pour the sauce over the shredded chicken and stir. Hold on Warm 10–15 minutes so it absorbs. Taste; add butter if it is too hot, a splash more vinegar if it reads flat.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"65A46A22-3329-53F2-817D-AEF4F404084C","order":8,"step":"During the last ~20 minutes, rinse 3 ¼ cups jasmine rice 2–3 times until the water runs mostly clear. Add to the Instant Pot with 3 ¼ cups water (1:1). Measure the water carefully — an over-filled pot gives waterlogged rice that packs soggy.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"83B84AD3-1B78-5EF1-87F9-1E6AA671449C","order":9,"step":"Confirm the valve is set to SEALING. Pressure Cook (Manual) on High for 3 minutes, natural release 10 minutes, then quick release. Fluff and leave the lid off to cool.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"E705D31A-4346-511A-AEE6-29DFD0B3369A","order":10,"step":"Microwave the frozen broccoli in its bags per the package. It is already blanched, so it needs steaming rather than cooking. Tip it into a colander and shake off the water.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"1C48E8CF-4204-587A-A11A-10D6679ADE88","order":11,"step":"Cool the chicken, rice, and broccoli 10–15 minutes before portioning. Sealing hot food causes condensation and sogginess.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"C3117F67-83D9-5B67-993E-FDA87371C43A","order":12,"step":"Assembly line across 10 open containers: 155 g chicken, then 148 g rice, then 100 g broccoli. No separate sauce container — the buffalo sauce is already in the chicken.","isSection":false},{"uuid":"0C671BDE-8938-5C08-95C3-17A8FC44C71B","order":13,"step":"Label with a dry-erase marker. 6 containers to the fridge, 4 to the freezer. Move freezer containers to the fridge the night before eating.","isSection":false}],"notes":"UNTESTED — v1, never cooked\n\nPER CONTAINER (10 total)\n  chicken: 155 g\n  rice: 148 g\n  broccoli: 100 g\n  total: 403 g\n\nSTORAGE: 6 fridge, 4 freezer\nFreezer containers move to the fridge the night before eating.\n\nFRESH TOPPINGS — NEVER PACKED: ranch or blue cheese dressing, diced celery\nAdded at eating time only.\n\nUNTESTED — quantities are planned, not observed. Weigh the shredded chicken\nafter step 5, the cooked rice after step 10, and the broccoli after step 11,\nthen promote with a real date.\n\nThis is built for a week with no time in it. Nothing touches an oven, there\nare no sheet pans to wash, and the only knife work is dicing celery at eating\ntime. The crockpot runs unattended for four to five hours.\n\n**Frozen broccoli is the deliberate choice, not a compromise.** Fresh crowns\nwould mean washing, trimming, cutting, oiling, two roasting batches and a\ndrain — 20–25 minutes, which is more than this recipe's entire hands-on\nbudget. Frozen florets are already blanched, so they only need steaming, and\n1000 g of frozen is 1000 g in the containers with no yield loss to plan\naround. Roasted tastes better; on a week like this it is not worth the time.\n\n**The sauce is cut to two-thirds and the tang rebuilt with vinegar.** Frank's\nRedHot is 190 mg of sodium per teaspoon, so the 1 ½ cups a full-strength\nversion calls for lands around 1500 mg per container — worse than the bottled\nteriyaki, and the worst number this rotation would have. ⅔ cup comes in near\n760 mg, under the ceiling.\n\nCutting hot sauce alone would leave it bland, so the 2 tbsp of white vinegar\nrestores the acidity and the cayenne restores the heat, neither of which\ncarries any sodium. Same move as the ground beef sauce: rebuild the flavour\nfrom unsalted components rather than accepting what the bottle gives you.\n\nIf you want the full-heat version, use 1 ½ cups Frank's and drop the vinegar\nand cayenne. It will be better buffalo and roughly 1500 mg of sodium, and the\nranch adds another ~260 mg on top at eating time.\n\n**Chicken is 5 ¼ lbs, not the 6 ½ an earlier draft suggested.** Chicken breast\nruns about 31 g of protein per 100 g against 26 for beef and turkey, so it\nneeds a smaller portion for the same protein. At 180 g per container this\ncomes to 62 g of protein, over the 45–55 band; 155 g lands at 54 g. Planned\nagainst the 0.65 crockpot yield in standing parameters, not the 0.76 that\ndraft assumed — 0.76 is the top of the observed range and the one measurement\nthis repo has is 0.637.\n\nRanch goes on at eating time, never packed — it separates when reheated.\nCelery diced fresh, not on prep day.","neutritionalInfo":"Serving Size: 1 container,\nCalories: 575 kcal,\nProtein: 54 g,\nCarbohydrates: 48 g,\nFat: 13 g,\nFiber: 4 g,\nSodium: 760 mg,\nSugar: 0 g","sourceName":"ten-containers","webLink":"https://zjbecker32.github.io/ten-containers/recipes/buffalo-chicken/","tags":[],"images":[]}